{"nodes": [{"id": "crates_pool_control_agents", "label": "crates/pool-control agent guide (AGENTS.md): the library that holds the authority rules of the control plane (start state, first bootstrap, writer admission) as plain functions over values; it reads no file, clock or socket and nothing calls it yet; scope 004 connects the journal, the probe and the clock", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "crates/pool-control/AGENTS.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "_origin": "semantic"}, {"id": "crates_pool_control_agents_key_files", "label": "pool-control key files: src/lib.rs (crate documentation and public names), src/authority.rs (StoreProbe, StoredAuthority, AuthorityState, Authority, classify_startup), src/bootstrap.rs (BootstrapPlan, BootstrapRefusal, plan_bootstrap), src/admission.rs (WriterAdmission, EligiblePrimary, Closed, ClosedReason, writer_admission), src/observation.rs (Observation, NodeFacts, TimelineId, MonotonicTime, the freshness rule), tests/walkthroughs.rs (the four walks of spec 0003 and the ac16_ tests), tests/admission_model.rs (the model test over 8192 cases)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "crates/pool-control/AGENTS.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "_origin": "semantic"}, {"id": "crates_pool_control_agents_commands", "label": "pool-control commands: cargo test -p pool-control --locked runs only this package's tests; the 0003 AC-11 grep for Instant::now, SystemTime, std::fs and std::env in crates/pool-control/src must print nothing", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "crates/pool-control/AGENTS.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "_origin": "semantic"}, {"id": "crates_pool_control_agents_authority_never_from_observation", "label": "pool-control convention: authority is never derived from an observation; writer_admission opens only when the configuration (expected_writer), the journal (the approved writer) and a fresh observation name the same node, and every other state ends closed (0001 SC-8, R-19)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "crates/pool-control/AGENTS.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "_origin": "semantic"}, {"id": "crates_pool_control_agents_private_constructors", "label": "pool-control convention: code outside the crate cannot build an Authority, an EligiblePrimary, a Closed or a BootstrapPlan; keep their fields private; each has a compile_fail doc test with a twin that compiles (0003 AC-12)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "crates/pool-control/AGENTS.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "_origin": "semantic"}, {"id": "crates_pool_control_agents_ready_belongs_to_its_configuration", "label": "pool-control convention: a Ready state belongs to the configuration it was classified with; writer_admission compares control.authority_id first and closes with one reason when it is missing or different (0003 AC-16)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "crates/pool-control/AGENTS.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "_origin": "semantic"}, {"id": "crates_pool_control_agents_time_passed_as_value", "label": "pool-control convention: the caller passes the time as a value; the freshness rule uses only the latest sample of a node; a sample dated after now, a stale one or a tie at the latest time counts as no evidence (0003 AC-11)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "crates/pool-control/AGENTS.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "_origin": "semantic"}, {"id": "crates_pool_control_agents_only_dependency_pool_config", "label": "pool-control convention: the only dependency is pool-config; the crate never depends on pool-core and has no dev-dependencies and no build script (0003 AC-13)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "crates/pool-control/AGENTS.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "_origin": "semantic"}, {"id": "crates_pool_control_agents_restart_rule_in_doc_comment", "label": "pool-control convention: every public record type states its restart rule in its documentation comment (0003 AC-14)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "crates/pool-control/AGENTS.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "_origin": "semantic"}, {"id": "crates_pool_control_agents_reason_names_are_contract", "label": "pool-control convention: the reason names, such as authority.uninitialized and authority.conflict_latched, are a contract; changing one is a decision in spec 0003", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "crates/pool-control/AGENTS.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "_origin": "semantic"}, {"id": "crates_pool_control_agents_gotcha_ready_is_a_copy", "label": "pool-control gotcha: a Ready state is a copy of the journal at the start and does not learn of a conflict latch set later, so the daemon of scope 004 must carry that (spec 0003 Follow-up 4)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "crates/pool-control/AGENTS.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "_origin": "semantic"}, {"id": "crates_pool_control_agents_gotcha_store_probe_public", "label": "pool-control gotcha: StoreProbe and StoredAuthority can be built by any crate; the guarantee of 0003 AC-12 holds only while the journal reader is the one code that builds them", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "crates/pool-control/AGENTS.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_